WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.168
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show"
starring

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.169
me, Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.637
Hi, everybody.
Happy Friday.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.373
Let's get some jokes here.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:08.574
Well, guys, this Sunday
is Mother's Day.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:11.577
Happy Mother's Day
to all the moms out there!

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:13.112
That's right, this Sunday
is Mother's Day,

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.647
but experts are telling people

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.682
not to visit their moms,
or hug them.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:18.918
In other words, they want us
to treat Mother's Day

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.953
like it's Father's Day.

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:23.589
You kids remembered?

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:26.759
You didn't?
[ Laughs ]

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.361
Of course, a lot of kids had
to serve their mom

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.963
breakfast in bed.
That's nice.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.597
It'd be special,
if you hadn't

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:34.300
eaten every meal in bed
for the past two months.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.668
It's the thought that counts.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:39.572
Meanwhile, I saw that 23&amp;Me
is offering a discount

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:43.276
on DNA testing kits
for Mother's Day, yeah.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:46.045
'Cause nothing says
"Mother's Day" like saying,

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.980
"Are you really my mom?

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.483
Let's really find out."

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.951
Have you ever done that?

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:52.951
-Never.

00:00:52.951 --> 00:00:54.053
I haven't done it either.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.655
-I'm scared to give it up.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.357
-Why?
-It goes into the system and...

00:00:58.357 --> 00:00:59.692
-Please.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.894
You're already in the system.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.795
-[ Chuckle ]

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.131
-[ Chuckle ] I'm in --
We're all in the system.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:08.101
[ Laughing ] Right now,
you're already in the system.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:11.171
-[ Laughing ]
-I just saw you walk by you.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.438
They've cloned you already.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:14.707
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.842
Check this out. Dunkin' Donuts
has started offering

00:01:16.842 --> 00:01:19.979
DIY donut kits
that come with a variety

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.347
of frosting and sprinkles.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.882
Take a look.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.083
It's perfect if you
want to give give your kids

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.318
a 30-second activity

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.020
and yourself an hour
of cleaning.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.990
That's right, you can make
your own Dunkin' Donuts at home

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.359
and, to make it authentic,
the first step is

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.262
to let the donuts sit
outside for 30 days.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.431
[ Laughs ]

00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:40.733
Oh, I saw that,
after the release

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.969
of Mountain Dew-flavored
Doritos, you can now buy

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:46.606
Mountain Dew
Baja Blast lip balm.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.275
Unfortunately, that's not all
Mountain Dew is coming out with.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.777
Take a look at this commercial.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.711
-Mountain Dew
is proud to introduce

00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:55.848
our new Mountain Dew
Baja Blast lip balm!

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.349
We ain't stoppin' there.

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:58.350
We got a whole slew

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.885
of Mountain Dew-inspired
products

00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:02.188
that'll get! you! amped!

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.824
I'm talkin'
Citrus Assault eye drops!

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.725
See the burn!

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:11.064
High-octane Berry Blast
Blizzard Tsunami Tylenol PM!

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.299
You're gonna sleep so hard!

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.635
Hey, Code Red toilet paper!

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.436
Flush it!

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:20.539
Mountain Dew!
The bath salts of soda!

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:22.475
Yeah!
[ Whip cracks ]

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.643
-Listen to this --
starting on Monday,

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.811
Amtrak will require
all passengers to wear

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.780
face masks or coverings.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.116
Meanwhile, Greyhound said
you can rip off

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.984
whatever fabric is left
on the seats

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:34.654
and make your own mask.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.522
I read that Google
told employees

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.124
that they can no longer
expense their lunch

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.293
while working from home.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.428
That's right,
Google made the change

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.931
after one --
Sorry. My phone's ringing.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.068
Pause it.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.837
[ Chuckle ] Hello.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:54.674
[ Laughs ]
Hi. It's Jimmy. How are ya?

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:58.077
-Jimmy.
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.579
This is --
-Why are you laughing?

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.547
-I'm laughing because I'm
in middle of my monologue.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.283
Would you mind if I put this
on speaker phone?

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.551
'Cause people aren't
gonna believe this.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.586
-[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:09.789
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:10.990
Here it is.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.159
[ Laughter ]
-Guys, this is --

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.295
This is Barbra --
-Recognize my laugh.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.696
-This is Barbra Streisand
on the phone.

00:03:17.696 --> 00:03:19.732
Hi! I'm so happy
you're calling.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.001
Happy belated birthday!
-Oh, well, you know,

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.736
what have I got to do all day?

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:27.373
You know.
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.308
Oh, my God.
-How are you doing?

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:30.810
What are you doing?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.344
-Ohhh!

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.480
How am I doing, Jimmy?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.717
Well, you know,
I just made this video

00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:40.786
and so I --
-Oh, I loved it, by the way.

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:41.787
I saw it.
-I just wondered if you saw it.

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.088
That's all.
-Ugh!

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:44.823
-"You'll Never Walk Alone"
is one of my favorites!

00:03:44.823 --> 00:03:46.892
And you're one of my favorites.

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:49.828
By the way, how do I know this
is the real Barbra Streisand?

00:03:49.828 --> 00:03:51.897
-How do you know?
-What's my favorite

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:53.465
Barb-- Yeah.
-Okay, okay.

00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:55.267
What is it?
What do you want to know?

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:57.503
-[ Laughing ] What's my favorite
Barbra Streisand song?

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.372
Would you know?
-I think -- I think it may be...

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:02.108
♪ People ♪
-[ Laughing ]

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.276
-♪ People who need people ♪

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:07.847
We all need each other now,
more than ever, don't we, Jimmy?

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:08.948
-Oh! We really do.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.184
I love
"You'll Never Walk Alone."

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.519
I'm a big fan of "Carousel"

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.287
and, obviously --
-Oh.

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:16.756
-I remember you did that.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.357
So you performed that song --

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:20.292
Was it after 9/11?

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:21.827
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:04:21.827 --> 00:04:24.363
What I did was integrate
that performance

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:27.066
with pictures of these amazing,

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:30.703
dedicated healthcare workers
that are risking their lives

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:34.540
every day during this crisis,
so, it's an ode to them

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.908
you know?
-It's beautiful.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.009
I did get to see it.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:39.311
I love that you did that.

00:04:39.311 --> 00:04:41.013
-Oh, good.
And it ends

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:44.049
with a title card
about Direct Relief,

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:46.785
which is an organization
that supplies

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:50.990
very much needed protective gear
to doctors and nurses, you know.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.792
-Yeah. We love Direct Relief.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.560
Actually, I can talk about this.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.629
This'll be on the show tonight,
if you don't mind.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:59.465
I could put a chyron so people
can donate to Direct Relief.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:00.666
-Oh, that's so nice.

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.000
That's really nice.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.502
Thank you for doing that.

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:06.338
-You've been doing amazing stuff
during this whole thing

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:08.641
and I'm thankful
that you're staying healthy

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.309
and staying at home.

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:12.312
Did you get to enjoy
your birthday at all?

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.382
-My birthday?
My birthday, I had a --

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:19.252
Well, we tried to have
a Zoom birthday,

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:20.586
but it was kind of a fiasco

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:23.155
because I'm very
technically challenged...

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:24.423
-[ Laughing ]
-...and I didn't know you had

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.525
to be close to the computer
when you're talking,

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:29.061
so nobody could hear me
and, you know.

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:30.496
My friends were more competent.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:33.433
They sent in little videos,
which my office put together,

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:36.969
so it was wonderful to see
everyone for like a few minutes

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:40.005
before I had to like say,
"This is ridiculous," you know?

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:43.175
-[ Laughs ] That's fantastic.
-So I decided that --

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:45.812
-Anyway.
-So, I have been home, you know,

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:48.347
just with my husband and my dog.

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:50.949
My dogs.
I have three of them now.

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:55.087
And my assistant of 47 years
is just amazing.

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:57.590
-Wow.
-But do you want to know

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.793
what I do during the day?
-Yeah. Like what happens

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:01.927
when you wake up?
-Okay.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:04.163
Well, I tweet
many times a day --

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.232
I don't know if you
follow me, but --

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:10.336
to express my feelings
about this administration

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:13.973
and what they're doing
and not doing, like testing.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:17.143
And then, I have to calm myself
down with coffee ice cream,

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.645
but it keeps me up at night,
so I can't sleep,

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:22.081
so I have to eat it
for breakfast,

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:23.983
but my breakfast is 12:00 noon

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.619
because I stay up till 4:00
in the morning, see?

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:27.987
-[ Laughs ]
-Reading the news

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:31.690
and researching companies
to invest in for my foundation.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:35.494
That's how I raise funds so I
can give money to great causes.

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:38.597
-You are fascinating
and you give to so many causes.

00:06:38.597 --> 00:06:40.432
You really do so much giving,

00:06:40.432 --> 00:06:43.268
which is an awesome thing
that you do.

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:46.338
-Well, I wanted to help
New York, so I, you know,

00:06:46.338 --> 00:06:50.076
gave a lot of PPE
to Mount Sinai in New York

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:52.577
'cause that's where
my son was born.

00:06:52.577 --> 00:06:54.413
And in L.A., it's UCLA

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:56.615
and Cedars-Sinai
and Saint John's,

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:58.951
'cause they need
medical equipment, you know?

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:02.321
-They really do.
-We're giving to organizations

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:07.192
that help people who are hungry,
like America's Food Fund

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:11.096
and Feeding America;
the World Health Organization,

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:12.764
which, we really need them...

00:07:12.764 --> 00:07:14.433
-Oh!
-...by the way, so.

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:17.203
I'm also thinking
about the next election

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:20.206
and I've been contributing
to organizations

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:23.108
like Rock the Vote,
Indivisible, America Votes,

00:07:23.108 --> 00:07:25.644
which help people
get registered

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:28.280
because we want to make sure
everyone can exercise

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.983
their right to vote
in November safely,

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:34.286
which means we need to make
it possible to vote by mail.

00:07:34.286 --> 00:07:35.454
You've heard
about all this, right?

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:36.989
-Yeah. You should mail in
your votes.

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:40.125
Get on it right now
and get it in there, yeah.

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:43.795
-You know, we have to do that
to ensure one person, one vote.

00:07:43.795 --> 00:07:46.165
We have to get rid of the
electoral college, too.

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:47.199
-Yeah.
-But am I talking too much...

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:48.767
-No! Not at all!
-...politics?

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:49.969
[ Laughs ]
-You can talk for the rest here.

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:51.737
I just love that you called.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.607
[ Laughing ] I happened
to be doing the monologue.

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:55.741
It wasn't that great
of a joke, either.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:56.842
I'm not even gonna
tell you what it was.

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:59.045
-What kind of monologue
are you doing

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:00.178
today?
-Oh, you know,

00:08:00.178 --> 00:08:03.615
I'm doing some Mother's Day
jokes, you know.

00:08:03.615 --> 00:08:07.819
I'm talking about, uh --
Amtrak jokes.

00:08:07.819 --> 00:08:09.021
There's nothing really --

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:11.323
-You're trying to --
Yeah, right.

00:08:11.323 --> 00:08:12.892
-I'm trying to make
people smile.

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:14.659
[ Laughs ]
-I think you're right.

00:08:14.659 --> 00:08:16.729
I think we have to laugh.

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:19.632
If not, you know,
we would be crying, so.

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:22.167
I think you're doing
a good job, honey.

00:08:22.167 --> 00:08:23.569
-Barbra, love you so much,

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:25.304
and maybe I'll give you
a call later.

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:28.074
We'll have some Zoom
cocktails for your birthday.

00:08:28.074 --> 00:08:31.310
-Okay, that one I just didn't
quite hear,

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.779
but what did you just say?
It broke up.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.214
-I'm gonna Zoom you later.

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:37.115
Maybe we'll have some cocktails
for your birthday.

00:08:37.115 --> 00:08:39.384
-No, don't Zoom me.
Call me on the phone

00:08:39.384 --> 00:08:41.487
because I'm not a Zoomer, okay?

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:43.388
-I love you so much.
-Have a good show, honey.

00:08:43.388 --> 00:08:45.023
-Thank you.
I will have a great show.

00:08:45.023 --> 00:08:46.659
Oh, my gosh, thank you so much.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:48.460
Good to hear from you, bud.
-You're so welcome.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.562
Love you. Bye-bye.
-Love you.

00:08:50.562 --> 00:08:54.033
[ Laughs ]

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:58.036
-I mean, legendary.
-Come on. Come on.

00:08:58.036 --> 00:09:00.139
-The best.

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.241
-That's so weird
'cause I put it in the thing.

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:04.443
I said I loved her.
"You Will Never Walk Alone,"

00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:06.211
which is one of my favorites
from "Carousel."

00:09:06.211 --> 00:09:10.216
I go, "I love Barbra Streisand.
I love her version of that song.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:13.119
And it's so fitting now. It's
moving. It'll make you cry."

00:09:13.119 --> 00:09:15.587
Shows all the people
working on the front lines.

00:09:15.587 --> 00:09:18.857
And so I just put --
See? She's magic.

00:09:18.857 --> 00:09:21.393
She is magical.

00:09:21.393 --> 00:09:22.795
Already the show's
off the rails.

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:26.999
This is the craziest show with
Bootsy and Bill Murray,

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:29.802
Mark Ruffalo,
Guy Fieri, Miranda Lambert.

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:32.605
Okay, let me
finish the monologue here.

00:09:32.605 --> 00:09:35.607
Listen to this. Starting on
Monday, Amtrak will require --

00:09:35.607 --> 00:09:37.142
[ Laughs ]

00:09:37.142 --> 00:09:40.346
I love that she called.

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:42.347
I read that Google
told employees

00:09:42.347 --> 00:09:45.317
that they can no longer expense
their lunch working from home.

00:09:45.317 --> 00:09:48.053
Google made the change
after one employee's lunch

00:09:48.053 --> 00:09:51.991
was a steak, a Nintendo Switch,
and a pool table.

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:53.259
And finally, I saw that

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:55.660
there's a new "Breaking Bad"
Monopoly board game.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.863
It's just like the regular game
except Mr. Monopoly

00:09:57.863 --> 00:10:00.132
is wearing tighty-whities
and a gas mask.

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:03.869
That is our monologue right
there and one for the books.

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:06.172
Oh, my goodness.

00:10:06.172 --> 00:10:08.106
Guys, it's time
for thank-you notes.

00:10:08.106 --> 00:10:12.545
-Jimmy always devotes time
for thank-you notes.

00:10:12.545 --> 00:10:14.947
-Alright, it's Friday.
I usually write out

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:16.715
my weekly thank-you
notes right now.

00:10:16.715 --> 00:10:20.586
So, I like to write out
my thank-you notes.

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:24.055
And so I was wondering,
Franny,

00:10:24.055 --> 00:10:26.325
can I get some thank-you note
writing music please?

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:28.761
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:32.631 line:0%
♪♪

00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:34.666
Thank you, grocery list in 2020,

00:10:34.666 --> 00:10:37.169
for looking like everyone's
from college --

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:41.607
frozen pizza,
Pop Tarts, and beer.

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:43.809
[ Laughter ]

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:47.079
Alright. Alright. Let's wait.

00:10:47.079 --> 00:10:49.915
Hold on. Don't overdo it, right?

00:10:49.915 --> 00:10:55.220
Alright, let's wait.
Alright, here we go.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.155
Thank you,
home-made Mother's Day cards,

00:10:57.155 --> 00:10:58.657
for letting kids show Mom

00:10:58.657 --> 00:11:01.660
they love her best way
they know how -- by drawing her

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:05.630
with 20 fingers per hand,
wings and bigger than the house.

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:11.136
[ Laughs ]

00:11:11.136 --> 00:11:12.104
Alright.

00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:14.406
Go to the next one.

00:11:14.406 --> 00:11:15.707
Thank you, Santa,

00:11:15.707 --> 00:11:19.712
for being the original
no-contact delivery person.

00:11:19.712 --> 00:11:24.449
Sorry, for being the original
no-contact delivery service.

00:11:24.449 --> 00:11:29.088
Sorry, there was no music,
and I got distracted as well.

00:11:29.088 --> 00:11:30.589 line:0%
♪♪

00:11:30.589 --> 00:11:34.726
Thank you,
wearing a skull face mask,

00:11:34.726 --> 00:11:36.795
for saying "I want to look like
I can rob you"

00:11:36.795 --> 00:11:39.130
while also letting you know that
I care about your grandma.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:42.034
-Winnie, move your hand.
Thank you.

00:11:42.034 --> 00:11:43.702
-Alright, go to the next one.

00:11:43.702 --> 00:11:47.406
And move your hand away.

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:49.508
Music.

00:11:49.508 --> 00:11:54.947
Thank you, Tom Cruise, signing
on to shoot a movie in space,

00:11:54.947 --> 00:11:57.983
for giving us chance
to see a blooper reel

00:11:57.983 --> 00:12:02.053
with the sound guy getting
sucked out of an airlock.

00:12:02.053 --> 00:12:06.692
[ Laughs ]
Go to the next one.

00:12:06.692 --> 00:12:09.861
[ Laughter ]

00:12:09.861 --> 00:12:15.267
-Thank you -- Thank you --

00:12:15.267 --> 00:12:20.806
[ Laughter ]

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.948
Alright, alright.

00:12:29.948 --> 00:12:31.916
One second. One second.
Let me try this one, ready?

00:12:31.916 --> 00:12:34.019
Stop. What are you doing?

00:12:34.019 --> 00:12:37.389
Thank you, "I had a crazy day,"
for now meaning

00:12:37.389 --> 00:12:40.325
"I ordered takeout
and I got the mail."

00:12:40.325 --> 00:12:41.960
Is that worth it?

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.730
Yep. Go, next one.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.365
Thank you, drive-through
birthday parties,

00:12:46.365 --> 00:12:48.333
for being a fun way for kids
to see their friends

00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:50.903
and a dream
come true for parents.

00:12:50.903 --> 00:12:53.205
Happy birthday, Monica,
and it's over.

00:12:53.205 --> 00:12:55.040
We don't have to stay two hours.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.377
Ah, we love you. Just go, guys.

00:12:58.377 --> 00:13:02.548 line:0%
♪♪

00:13:02.548 --> 00:13:06.251
Thank you, social distancing,
for doing the impossible --

00:13:06.251 --> 00:13:12.491
making me nostalgic
about elevator small talk.

00:13:12.491 --> 00:13:16.295
[ Laughter ]

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:22.033
-Next?

00:13:22.033 --> 00:13:24.636
Next?
-Yep.

00:13:24.636 --> 00:13:27.773
-Franny, quit wasting our time!

00:13:27.773 --> 00:13:29.775
-Wow, let's go. Here we go.

00:13:29.775 --> 00:13:33.345
Thank you. Go, last one.

00:13:33.345 --> 00:13:36.281
Thank you, buying Cinco de
Mayo margaritas by the gallon,

00:13:36.281 --> 00:13:39.251
for letting us experience
hangovers family style.

00:13:39.251 --> 00:13:40.152
There you go.

00:13:40.152 --> 00:13:46.425
[ Laughter ]

00:13:46.425 --> 00:13:47.593
That's "Thank You Notes,"
everybody.

